@bank all
// SW4's words for the eight 0.92.6 traditions' join cards (TB4's build, claude/p995-trad926, behind TRAD926_JOIN_ON),
// from TB4's stand-ins in T926_CARD. Keys (section 18, the Traditions slot):
//   t932.<id>.join      the host's greeting when you tap them (one a day, by the day)
//   t926.<id>.ask       the host's question, the Mail's promise
//   t926.<id>.pick.N    your three answers (N 1-3); t926.<id>.answer.N the host's reply to answer N (one line each, so
//                       a pick and its answer always match)
//   t926.tool-night.right / .wrong   Kovac, after you name the tool in your hand ({tool}: "a torque wrench")
//   t926.garden-walk.done            the end of the walk (narration, as the lap's)
//   t932.<id>.close     the host, near the end (a bubble, once)
// Each host in their own voice (content/voices/); Window sketching's two hosts (Luca Alvarez; Lumi Achebe, no card,
// written plainly) get a set each. No line here repeats a tradition's own ask/here lines.

// tool-night (host kovac-zainab): shy, exact, quietly funny
== t932.tool-night.join
- Oh. You came. Um. Hands out, eyes shut. I'll put one in your palm.
- Hi. Sit there. Eyes closed, please. Properly closed. I'll know.
== t926.tool-night.ask
- Feel the weight. Feel the end of it. What is it?
== t926.tool-night.right
- Yes. That's {tool}. Sorry, I mean, well named. Next one's harder.
== t926.tool-night.wrong
- Um. Not quite. That was {tool}. It fools everyone. It fooled me once.
== t932.tool-night.close
- Last tool back in its row. All of them where they live. Thank you.
- That's every one named. I'll sort them again later. Don't tell anyone.

// route-night (host raman): soft and exact; flies like carrying soup
== t932.route-night.join
- Ah, hello. Here's your pin. Hold it by the head. The table's been dusted.
- Good to see you. The week's laid out. Take a pin, and take your time.
== t926.route-night.ask
- Seven days from now. Where do you think she'll be? Show me with the pin.
== t926.route-night.pick.1
- Just past the dust.
== t926.route-night.pick.2
- Halfway to the next beacon.
== t926.route-night.pick.3
- Right on the line you drew.
== t926.route-night.answer.1
- A bold guess. The dust slows us more than people think. We'll see.
== t926.route-night.answer.2
- Halfway. That's a careful pin. I'd have put mine near there.
== t926.route-night.answer.3
- Kind of you. The line's only a hope, mind. She goes where it's safe.
== t932.route-night.close
- Pins stay in till next time. Then we'll know who was closest.
- That's the week. Gentle turns, all of them. Goodnight.

// card-night (host oduya): unhurried, warm, knows every birthday
== t932.card-night.join
- Hello, hello. Pull up a chair. A few birthdays are coming, and each one wants a card.
- Come in, come in. Paper's in the middle, glue's going round. Whose? I'm not saying.
== t926.card-night.ask
- Before you start, what are you going to put on the front?
== t926.card-night.pick.1
- A rocket. A wonky one.
== t926.card-night.pick.2
- The Wren, with everyone waving.
== t926.card-night.pick.3
- Gold pen. Lots of gold pen.
== t926.card-night.answer.1
- A wonky rocket. I know someone who'll keep that on their shelf for years.
== t926.card-night.answer.2
- Everyone waving. That one might make somebody quiet for a moment. In a good way.
== t926.card-night.answer.3
- Go gently with the gold. It's the one everybody wants, and there's only the one.
== t932.card-night.close
- Leave them with me. I'll get each one to the right person on the right day.
- That's a good pile. Somebody's going to have a lovely morning.

// garden-walk (host cruz-tove, they/them): mumbles to people, chats to plants, dates by sowing week
== t932.garden-walk.join
- Mm, hello. Slowly. They don't like being rushed. Nor do I.
- Oh. Hi. Walk behind me. Mind the edges. The edges are new.
== t926.garden-walk.ask
- One leaf each. You pick. Not... well. You know which not.
== t926.garden-walk.pick.1
- The basil.
== t926.garden-walk.pick.2
- One of the lettuces.
== t926.garden-walk.pick.3
- That red one. The chilli.
== t926.garden-walk.answer.1
- Basil. Week six. Rub it first, then eat it. There. That's the good bit.
== t926.garden-walk.answer.2
- That's a week-five one. Crunchy still. Hello, lettuce. Sorry.
== t926.garden-walk.answer.3
- No. Not the chillies. The Mail said. Here, a leaf of mint instead.
== t926.garden-walk.done
- Every bed with Cruz, slowly, and back to the start. You could nearly tell the weeks now.
== t932.garden-walk.close
- That's all of them. They liked the company. Mm. So did I.
- Back where we began. Same beds next time. Bigger.

// window-sketch (host alvarez-luca): cheerful and silly, says hello to things
== t932.window-sketch.join
- Hiya! Pencils on the sill, paper on the cushion. Wave at the stars first. Manners.
- Hey, hey! Grab a pencil. Nobody looks at anybody's till the end.
== t926.window-sketch.ask
- Ooh, what are you doing? Tell me before you start.
== t926.window-sketch.pick.1
- Tavessa. The smudge.
== t926.window-sketch.pick.2
- The stars. Every one.
== t926.window-sketch.pick.3
- The bit of hull you can see.
== t926.window-sketch.answer.1
- Everyone's smudge comes out different. Mine looks like a sheep. Every time.
== t926.window-sketch.answer.2
- Every one! Ambitious. Start with the bright one and see how far you get.
== t926.window-sketch.answer.3
- Nobody draws the hull! I love it. That's going on the wall.
== t932.window-sketch.close
- Pencils down! Hold them up. Oh, look at them all. Lovely.
- Time's up. Say goodbye to the stars. They'll be there next time.

// window-sketch-2 (host achebe-lumi, no voice card): plain and friendly
== t932.window-sketch-2.join
- Hello. Paper's there, pencils are there. Draw whatever's out of the window.
- Oh, good, another one. Find a bit of window and start anywhere.
== t926.window-sketch-2.ask
- What are you going to try?
== t926.window-sketch-2.pick.1
- That faint smudge. Tavessa.
== t926.window-sketch-2.pick.2
- As many stars as I can fit.
== t926.window-sketch-2.pick.3
- That curve of hull by the frame.
== t926.window-sketch-2.answer.1
- The smudge. Soft pencil for that, and don't press. It's mostly not there.
== t926.window-sketch-2.answer.2
- All of them? Dots, then. Lots of little dots, and no rubbing out.
== t926.window-sketch-2.answer.3
- The hull. Hardly anyone does. It's a good shape, once you look.
== t932.window-sketch-2.close
- Pencils down. Keep yours, or leave it on the sill for the wall.
- That's time. Same window, next time.

// open-house (host ferreira): quick and bright, a born host, never repeats a message
== t932.open-house.join
- Hello, hello! Come in. Be nosy, it's allowed today. Only today.
- There you are! Coats off, eyes open. Ask me anything except what's in the messages.
== t926.open-house.ask
- So. Where shall we start?
== t926.open-house.pick.1
- The relay queue.
== t926.open-house.pick.2
- The old log.
== t926.open-house.pick.3
- Can I try the headset?
== t926.open-house.answer.1
- There it is. Counts and times, that's all you'll see. What's inside each one stays sealed.
== t926.open-house.answer.2
- Chief Holt keeps that. He'll turn the pages for you. Gloves, please. Obrigada.
== t926.open-house.answer.3
- For a minute. Listen, don't speak, and leave the dial alone. Everyone tries the dial.
== t932.open-house.close
- Doors close in a minute! Thank you for being nosy. It's nice to be visited.
- That's the tour. Now you know where the voices come from.

// spoon-band (host rossi-femi): bright and keen, one exclamation mark, everything a race
== t932.spoon-band.join
- Hello! Grab something that rattles. First to find a beat wins.
- Hi, hi. Sit in. Anything that makes a noise counts. Even you.
== t926.spoon-band.ask
- Quick, before I count us in: what are you playing?
== t926.spoon-band.pick.1
- Two spoons.
== t926.spoon-band.pick.2
- The pan lid.
== t926.spoon-band.pick.3
- The jar of rice.
== t926.spoon-band.answer.1
- Spoons! Back to back, tap them on your knee. Race me to the end of the song.
== t926.spoon-band.answer.2
- Pan lid. Loudest job going. Only on the big beats, or the whole wing will hear.
== t926.spoon-band.answer.3
- The rice! Shake on my count. I tried to learn the Veyli for shake. It went.
== t932.spoon-band.close
- Last song! Whoever finishes last wins. That's the rule tonight.
- That's us! Same band next time. Same spoons, if nobody bends them.

// worst-joke (host holt): gruff, few words, "Hm.", dry by accident; he has never laughed
== t932.worst-joke.join
- Hm. Cadet. You've brought one. Sit. When I nod, you start.
- There you are. Rules: one joke, said clearly. No explaining it after.
== t926.worst-joke.ask
- Go on. Your worst.
== t926.worst-joke.pick.1
- Why did the airlock break up? It needed space.
== t926.worst-joke.pick.2
- What's a spanner's favourite song? Bolt from the blue.
== t926.worst-joke.pick.3
- I've got one about the reactor. It's not very hot.
== t926.worst-joke.answer.1
- Hm. Space. That's dreadful. Note the groan at the back. Adequate.
== t926.worst-joke.answer.2
- Bolt from the blue. I'll be hearing that on patrol. Thank you. I think.
== t926.worst-joke.answer.3
- That isn't a joke. That's a weather report. Sit down. I'm not smiling.
== t932.worst-joke.close
- Last joke. Then the judging. My face is the same as it was. Note that.
- Hm. The groans were loud tonight. I did not laugh. Write that down.
